Changes in v6:
- mask the failing queue too on the setup_rx enable-fail unwind: the
  rollback loop used while (--i), so queue i stayed unmasked across
  the napi_disable wait. It now remasks and synchronizes queues 0..i,
  and err_disable_napi remasks after napi_disable the way cleanup does
- drop WARN_ON() on ibmveth_toggle_irq() returns; the helper already
  logs the hcall rc, and rate-limit that print
- reword schedule_rx_queue() kdoc: true means NAPI was scheduled and
  the mask attempted; a failed disable_irq() is logged by the helper
  and does not change the return, and an out-of-range qindex returns
  false without being a prep failure. Masking still happens only when
  prep succeeds
- clarified: no standalone Fixes: tag. The hang the opened gate closes
  is now named in the body, but the fix depends on the helpers, flags
  and queue_irq[] added here, so it is not backportable alone
- noted: open-fail without h_free_logical_lan on pool-fail predates
  this patch, the LAN is registered before the buffer pools. The
  opened gate does remove the accidental h_free recovery a later
  ndo_stop used to give after a failed reopen. P06 orders h_free
  before the pool DMA and P07 moves pools ahead of register_rx_queues
- noted: the early !opened return can skip TX LTB free only if
  set_channels allocates while the adapter is closed, which v5 allowed
  by keying on IFF_UP. P14 gates set_channels on opened and P15
  publishes the RX count and CMO while down without allocating. close
  still frees TX LTBs whenever opened was true
- noted: per-queue poll() and enable_irq(qindex) land in P08, where
  the buffer-submit helper first needs a queue index, and the range
  check in P09; both before MQ is enabled in P10. Here the handler
  already passes &napi[i], but only napi[0] is registered

Changes in v5:
- Remask+sync after napi_disable in cleanup (in-flight poll can re-arm)
- Interrupt: quiet IRQ_NONE on out-of-range qindex (no WARN storm)
- Opened / rx_irq_setup gate cleanup so close after a failed open
  cannot napi_disable / free_irq without a prior enable/request; set
  opened on successful open; rx_irq_setup only on full setup success
- H_PARAMETER fold disable-only; enable stays error (stuck-masked visible)
- IRQ helpers return 0 / negative errno only (never raw H_* to ethtool)
- Decision: keep open IRQ order request_irq -> napi_enable while PHYP
  stays masked until schedule/enable (coherent with later scale-up)
- schedule_rx_queue returns bool (napi_schedule_prep success)
- Keep mask-only-on-prep-success (no else-mask; avoids idle+masked race)
- Call out free_irq-before-free_lan as intentional once PHYP is masked
- Poll re-arm during teardown lands with SQ poll-harden (not claimed here)
- synchronize_net() after RX IRQ/NAPI teardown in close
- Add subordinate IRQ dispose helpers (per-queue + bulk 1..N; bound to MAX)

Changes in v4:
- Include irq.h / irqdomain.h with first irq_dispose_mapping() use.
- Introduce IRQ helpers in the same patch that wires open/close/poll
  callers, instead of leaving unused statics.
- Factor process-context RX kicks into ibmveth_schedule_rx_queue();
  keep ibmveth_interrupt() as the IRQ-only wrapper.
- On cleanup, mask PHYP and synchronize_irq before napi_disable
  (storm-safety; not fully behavior-preserving vs classic close).
- Leave queue_irq[0] set after cleanup (queue 0 uses netdev->irq;
  next open reuses it). Only subordinate virqs are disposed.
